tags: network-bytes, net_mu_per_gib

A rate of the node: the price of the traffic that the node relays for an instance
through ServiceTunnel, for each GiB.

The value is MU for one GiB (2^30 bytes). Example: 50000. The bytes of the two
directions add. The node charges in proportion, and rounds each charge down to a whole
MU.

The rate has no scope. A reader that does not know the rate ignores it.

=== formal
base=1073741824 bytes
class=rate
name=network-bytes
of=the bytes that the node relays through ServiceTunnel for an instance, the two directions added
rounding=the node computes each charge in proportion and rounds it down to a whole MU
scope=none
